---
import { SITE } from '@/config/site';

const socials = [
  { href: SITE.links.youtube, label: 'YouTube' },
  { href: SITE.links.instagram, label: 'Instagram' },
  { href: SITE.links.whatsapp, label: 'WhatsApp' },
].filter((link) => link.href.length > 0);

/**
 * Licensing footnote.
 *
 * The repository link is the AGPL-3.0 section 13 offer of Corresponding Source, and it lives in
 * the shared footer deliberately: serving a modified version of this site over a network obliges
 * you to give its users the source of YOUR version, so putting the offer in the template every
 * page renders means a fork inherits the mechanism instead of having to remember it. A fork
 * repoints SITE.repository — never the two licence URLs below, which must keep pointing at the
 * licence texts themselves.
 *
 * The second sentence exists because unlabelled content reads as "all rights reserved": a teacher
 * who would happily print the worksheets otherwise never learns that they may.
 *
 * data-pagefind-ignore is belt-and-braces. The footer already escapes the index because
 * data-pagefind-body scopes indexing to the lesson bodies, but this text repeats on all 28 routes,
 * so were that scoping ever to move, every page would become a match for words nobody is searching
 * for. Same reasoning as the attribute on 404.astro and offline.astro.
 */
const AGPL_URL = 'https://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0.html';
const CC_URL = 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/deed.pt-BR';

const linkClass = 'text-brand-700 underline underline-offset-2';
---

<footer class="mt-16 border-t border-ink-100 bg-surface-alt">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4 py-8 text-sm text-ink-700">
    <p class="font-semibold text-ink-900">{SITE.name}</p>
    <p class="mt-1 max-w-prose">{SITE.description}</p>

    {
      socials.length > 0 && (
        <ul class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-4">
          {socials.map((link) => (
            <li>
              <a class={linkClass} href={link.href}>
                {link.label}
              </a>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      )
    }

    <p class="mt-6 max-w-prose text-ink-500">
      Seu progresso fica salvo apenas neste aparelho. Não pedimos cadastro e não guardamos seus
      dados em nenhum servidor.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-3 max-w-prose text-ink-500" data-licence data-pagefind-ignore>
      O código deste site é público e fica no <a
        class={linkClass}
        href={SITE.repository}
        rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a
      >, sob a licença <a class={linkClass} href={AGPL_URL} rel="noopener noreferrer">AGPL-3.0</a> — quem
      publicar uma versão modificada precisa deixar o código dela público também. Você pode imprimir,
      compartilhar e adaptar as aulas e as fichas, desde que dê crédito e não use para fins comerciais:
      é o que diz a licença <a class={linkClass} href={CC_URL} rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a
      >.
    </p>
  </div>
</footer>
